1.5 Race
Brunei Darussalam has a multi -ethnic population, categorised into three main racial groups
namely Brunei Malays, Chinese and Others. In the 2021 Census, Brunei Malays continued to
be the predominant racial group, accounting for 6 7.4 per cent (297,016 persons) of the total
population. The racial groups of Chinese and others comprised 9.6 per cent ( 42,132 persons)
and 23.0 per cent (101,567 persons) of the population respectively.
The Brunei Malays is categorised into seven ethnic groups, whereby Melayu Brunei had the
highest population (82.1 per cent or 243,782 persons). This was followed by Melayu Tutong
(5.9 per cent or 17,563 persons), Melayu Kedayan (5.6 per  or 16,617 persons) and the
remaining with less than 5.0 per cent; Melayu Dusun, Melayu Belait, Melayu Murut and
Melayu Bisaya (Chart 1.7). Meanwhile, Chinese and Others comprised of 9.6 per cent (42,132
persons) and 23.0 per  cent (101,567 persons) of the total population respectively . Others
include Malays from Malaysia and Indonesia, and other races from other countries such as
Bangladesh, Thailand, etc.
Chart 1.7: Population by Race, 2021, Brunei Darussalam

