1.6 Religion
Islam is the official religion of Brunei Darussalam and is embraced by the majority of the
country’s population, comprising of 82.1 per cent (362,035 persons) in 2021. This was higher
than the proportion of 78.8 per cent in 20 11. The remaining population consisted of 6.7 per
cent (29,462 persons) Christians, 6.3 per cent (27,745 persons) Buddhists and 4.9 per cent
(21,473 persons) were members of other faiths or having no religious beliefs (Chart 1.8).
Chart 1.8: Population by Religion, 2021, Brunei Darussalam

